    - rid: 7865913011368886595
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -1221.4192, y: 443.84082}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 15134834976047125082
          m_Value1: 7451722965250884038
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'This HP threshold node has an "Abort Target"

          of none. This
          means that nothing will happen

          at the moment the enemy drops
          to 50%, but

          rather the next time the enemy selects a move,

          this
          option will become available.'
    - rid: 7865913011368886632
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -899.84174, y: 396.6756}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 4148627016891837540
          m_Value1: 2578599644773322670
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'Conversely, the Abort Target of "Both" will

          cause the graph
          to immediately begin trying to

          activate this ability when the
          condition is met. It

          is important to note that the graph will
          parse

          from left to right, so especially with abilities that

          can
          overtake others it is imperative to ensure that

          the highest
          priority abilities are on the left side

          of the graph.


          When
          using an Abort Target of "Both", ensure that

          the "Immediately"
          bool of the ability is set to true.

          This is currently the only
          instance that "Immediately"

          should be set to true.'
