    - rid: 7865913068295553859
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -1823.8837, y: 570.093}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 6259719859501108992
          m_Value1: 7812835138104436829
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'Selects a random node from those

          linked beneath. For most
          enemies

          with simplistic AI, this will likely be

          the
          driving force for all of their logic.'
    - rid: 7865913068295553932
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -1556.9543, y: 568.1838}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 15071473936950536990
          m_Value1: 1368564599952463708
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'Tries all connected nodes in order from

          left to right.
          Useful if an enemy should

          only use a move if a certain condition
          is met.

          (Note: This node can be used to point to a

          "Random"
          node and a "Pass If" node,

          allowing for a specific move to be
          used if a

          codition is met, and random selection if the

          condition
          is not met.'
    - rid: 7865913070587216093
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: 297.21613, y: -111.06514}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 9397872135839728003
          m_Value1: 6808918883481279534
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'We want to make sure "Repeat" is turned off here. Otherwise, our

          StartOfCombat
          Abilities would loop repeatedly. We want the enemy to

          continue
          attacking due to a "Repeat" node further down the graph.'
    - rid: 7865913070587216414
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -2138.5913, y: 562.5132}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 2103062906275701490
          m_Value1: 12223401714848442275
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'Enemies will now begin charging a new ability

          after finishing
          charging the previoius ability

          + AttackCooldown, as opposed
          to previously,

          where an an attack needed to completely

          finish
          + AttackCooldown. This can result in the

          player having little
          time to react/recover once

          an enemy uses a powerful or large
          attack. To

          remedy this, you can provide a buffer after an

          attack
          by utilizing a "Wait for seconds" node right

          after that specific
          attack.'
    - rid: 7865913070587216415
      type: {class: ActionNodeModel, ns: Unity.Behavior, asm: Unity.Behavior.Authoring}
